UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|East should consider playing the @DJ at trick 1, which does beat the hand. True, I might have the @DQ, but in that case it doesn't matter. And if partner has the DQ (which he does) then it makes a big difference. |
PG| ***** 10 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In general, if partner leads a suit and there is a king or queen on the board, and you hold the AJ, the J is almost always right. You want to have your aces capture kings and queens if at all possible.|
PG| ***** 11 ***** |


