%%%%%%Hand 3
https://tinyurl.com/224mq3ay
qx|A3|st||rh||ah|Board 3 IMPs   -   July 31, 2024|pn|hondo717,IraCT,danpsych,Sputniks|
md|1SKJ75H6DK653CAQ43,SA8HKQT74DAQ8CK62,S94HJ98DJT92CJT87,SQT632HA532D74C95|sv|e|
mb|1C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|With my hand most players open 1@D with 4-4 in the minors and that is okay. But I prefer to open 1@C unless I have weak clubs and nice diamonds because it gives more flexibility to the auction. However, that is non-standard (although recommended by Marty Bergen).|
PG| ***** 30 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|MB|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|West has at least 3 choices of bids. they are double, 1@H, and 1NT. Each is flawed but I like double. Doubling and correcting to 2@H which shows a strong hand at least 16 but usually a 6-card suit. 1@H is a bit of an underbid and 1NT is also a bit of an underbid. |
PG| ***** 31 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|1NT shows 15-18 but with the 5-card heart suit with 3 honors, the hand is really worth more than 18. So my order of preference is double, with 1N a close second, and 1@H a distant third choice.|
PG| ***** 32 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BWest: ^*nMy other choice was 2NT.|
PG| ***** 33 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|2N is a bit of an overbid IMO while 1N is a bit of an underbid.|
PG| ***** 34 ***** |


mb|D|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|1S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I agree with 1@S, but East is almost strong enough to jump to 2@S showing 8-11. And 2N over 1@C on this auction is unusual.|
PG| ***** 35 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|2H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Now the 2@H bid is a double and correct showing 6 hearts or 5 very good hearts and at least 16. East should just bid 4@H with such nice support and a very possible 10 card fit. East can't have a much better hand given she bid 1@S to start with.|
PG| ***** 36 ***** |


mb|P|mb|4H|mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 37 ***** |


