UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Well played by West.|
PG| ***** 51 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BA Kib: ^*nIn the bidding when responding to a double, you are showing points more than shape.|
PG| ***** 52 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Yes the hand is worth 20 which is why I liked double and correct a bit better than 1N overcall. |
PG| ***** 53 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In responding to a takeout double, with less than an invitational hand (9 or a good 8) you just bid your best suit at the cheapest level. With an invitational hand (9-11 or so) you jump in your suit. With an opening hand you cue bid the opponents suit (2@C here). |
PG| ***** 54 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So the 1@S bid by East was correct as it is not quite an invitational hand although close, assuming partner has spades. Most of the time partner will have spades on this auction with a takeout double.|
PG| ***** 55 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|East's |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=dummypoints,Bergen Dummy Points ^*N|CP||FP||at| are 6 HCP, 1 length point, 1 point for the 2 doubletons, and 1 point for the 4-card side heart suit. So 2@S would not be unreasonable but probably a tad aggressive.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
