mb|P|mb|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|My choices are pass (although we could easily be in a 7-card fit), 2@H which shows a doubleton heart (since I didn't raise right away), or 2N which shows a good 10 or so. With several intermediates I like 2N slightly better than 2@H, although I usually prefer 2@H over 2N.|
PG| ***** 59 ***** |


mb|2N|mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 60 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|
pc|D3|pc|D7|pc|DQ|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The @DQ at trick one is not terrible but it hides the @DA from partner. If partner has the @DK (very possible) it doesn't matter. However, if he doesn't he may get confused. I think the best defense is to play the @DA and lead back a low diamond (low from the remaining count of 3 diamonds). I will play the Jack.|
PG| ***** 61 ***** |


