UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|As you can see, 3N was their best spot. 5@C is down 1 which is often the case. There are few hands where you prefer to be in 5 of a minor rather than 3N and you often can't figure out even if that is the case. |
PG| ***** 87 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The main time you end up in 5 of a minor is if you know for sure you lack a stopper in one suit. Otherwise you almost always prefer 3N over 5 of a minor.|
PG| ***** 88 ***** |


